What You Learned Today (Day 07)
1. The Power of Context in Prompting
You learned the difference between a generic prompt (Prompt A) and a context-rich prompt (Prompt B). The core lesson: 30 seconds of context transforms Claude from a content generator into a personal advisor.
2. Prompt Engineering Principles

Placeholders like [Student] are not context — filled-in details are
Context anchors every decision: which projects, which resources, what to skip
More specific input = more personalized, actionable output

3. Claude Model Tiers
You explored all three Claude models and when to use each:

Haiku 4.5 → Fast, simple tasks
Sonnet 4.6 → Daily workhorse (your primary model)
Opus 4.7 → Deep reasoning, hard problems

4. Effort Levels in Claude
Low / Standard / High / Max — and when to switch based on task importance.

5. Building a Personalized 30-Day Learning Roadmap
You saw how a roadmap shifts when built around your real profile (student, HTML/CSS done, JS next, job goal) versus a generic one.

6. Claude Usage Strategy
You built your own Claude usage strategy: which model to use for which task, when to increase effort, and the biggest mistakes to avoid.
